course: dictionary
lesson: 73
title: Acrobat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An acrobat is a performer who does difficult and exciting moves, such as flips, balancing and jumps. Acrobats are most often seen in a circus, but the word can also describe any creature or person who moves with great skill.
explain: Read the words around the word to understand it. «Squirrels are skilled acrobats that solve puzzles to reach bird feeders.» The word skilled and the puzzles tell you that acrobats are clever and quick, and that they can move in tricky ways.
explain: Look at the details in the next example. «Gibbons, the acrobats of Asian forests, are smaller apes with no tail too.» The forest is not a circus, so here acrobats means animals that swing and leap with great skill. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: An acrobat is a performer who does difficult, exciting movements.
fact: Acrobats often do flips, balancing and jumps, especially in a circus.
fact: Phrases you may meet: circus acrobat, trapeze acrobat, and a natural acrobat, which means someone who is gifted at acrobatic moves.
fact: «Squirrels» can be called skilled acrobats because they solve puzzles to reach food.
fact: «Gibbons» are smaller apes with no tail, and they are called the acrobats of Asian forests.
exercise: «Squirrels are skilled acrobats that solve puzzles to reach bird feeders.» Which meaning fits acrobats here? | A person who cooks food | A bird that sings loudly | *An agile animal that makes quick, clever moves | A tool for opening locks
exercise: «Gibbons, the acrobats of Asian forests, are smaller apes with no tail too.» What does acrobats suggest about gibbons? | They live only in circuses | *They swing and leap with great skill and speed | They have very long tails | They are slow and rarely move
exercise: «Gibbons, the acrobats of Asian forests, are smaller apes with no tail too.» Which group are gibbons part of? | Cats of the jungle | *Apes with no tail | Birds of the forest | Monkeys with long tails
test: A «trapeze acrobat» works high above the circus ring. What is a trapeze acrobat? | A clown who makes people laugh | *A performer who does daring moves on a swinging bar | A cook who bakes bread for the crowd | A driver of the circus lorry
test: Your friend says, «She is a natural acrobat, she did a backflip at once.» What does natural acrobat mean? | She works in the circus kitchen | She is afraid of heights | She practised for years before her first flip | *She has a gift for flips and balancing
exam: Which sentence uses acrobat correctly? | The acrobat cooked a pie for the audience | The acrobat's car needs a new tyre | *The tightrope walker was a brilliant acrobat, flipping across the wire | Our dog is a fine acrobat, he barks at the post
